<title>BELGIUM: EU clears British aid to Korean units in Wales.</title>
<headline>EU clears British aid to Korean units in Wales.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Wednesday it had approved British state aid of 247 million pounds ($407.3 million) to help co-finance investment projects by LG Electronics Wales Ltd (LGEW) and LG Semicon Wales Ltd (LGSW), owned by South Korean industrial conglomerate LG Engineering.</p>
<p>LGEW is among other things to invest 521 million pounds in the creation of a television and computer monitor production plant, and later in the assembly of colour display tubes and colour picture tubes for monitors.</p>
<p>LGSW, which operates in the semi-conducter industry, plans to invest 1.1 billion pounds in a plant.</p>
<p>The Commission said that the investments would not create over-capacity on the markets. It also noted that they would help create 6,100 jobs in south Wales.</p>
<p>-- Brussels newsroom +32 2 287 68 11 ($ = 0.606 British Pounds)</p>
